 "/docs/concepts": [
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Four ideas, nested inside each other. Once these are straight, the rest of the product is discoverable."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "depth": 2,
   "text": "Workspace",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Workspace"
    }
   ],
   "id": "workspace"
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "A workspace is the outermost container. It holds clusters and it holds people."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Your personal workspace is created for you automatically — the first time you sign in, and also the first time you create a board through the API without naming a workspace. You never have to set one up."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "You can belong to more than one workspace. The switcher at the top of the sidebar moves between them, and separates ones you own from ones shared with you."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "depth": 2,
   "text": "Cluster (board)",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Cluster (board)"
    }
   ],
   "id": "cluster-board"
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "A cluster is the unit of work: a moodboard, a scene, a project, a shot list."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "The interface calls it a "
    },
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "v": "cluster",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "cluster"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": ". The API, the database and the developer pages in these docs call the same object a "
    },
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "v": "board",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "board"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": ". This is a naming change that landed in the product before it landed in the code, and rather than pretend otherwise, both words appear here — "
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "cluster"
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": " when describing the interface, "
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "board"
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": " when describing an API payload."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Clusters nest without limit. A cluster inside a cluster is just a card on the parent's canvas that happens to open into its own canvas. This is how a project becomes a folder tree without anybody deciding to build a folder tree."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "note",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Nesting is cycle-safe. Dragging a cluster into one of its own descendants is refused rather than silently creating a loop."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "depth": 2,
   "text": "Card",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Card"
    }
   ],
   "id": "card"
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "A card is one thing on a board. Images, notes, links, documents, PDFs, video, audio, colour palettes, shapes, grids, schedules, votes, and other clusters are all cards."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Cards carry a position, a size and a stacking order, which is what makes the canvas a canvas rather than a list. Everything else about a card depends on what kind it is — see "
    },
    {
     "t": "link",
     "v": "Cards",
     "href": "/docs/canvas/cards",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "Cards"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "The free Demo plan allows "
    },
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "v": "100 cards",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "100 cards"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": " in total across every cluster you create. Clusters themselves are unlimited, and so are collaborators."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "depth": 2,
   "text": "Two views of the same cluster",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Two views of the same cluster"
    }
   ],
   "id": "two-views-of-the-same-cluster"
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Every cluster has two views, and they are not two places:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "strong",
      "v": "Canvas",
      "children": [
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "Canvas"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " — the infinite surface. Position matters. This is where you arrange, connect, draw and compare."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "strong",
      "v": "List",
      "children": [
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "List"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " — the same contents as a sortable, searchable file browser with table and gallery modes. This is where you find a specific thing."
     }
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Switching views does not move or convert anything. A cluster is one set of contents with two ways to look at it, which is why the product describes every cluster as also being a drive."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "depth": 2,
   "text": "What is not a container",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "What is not a container"
    }
   ],
   "id": "what-is-not-a-container"
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": "Two things look like containers and are not:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "v": "Groups",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "Groups"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": " are a selection on a canvas given a name and an outline. They travel together and can be commented on and tagged as a unit, but they do not have their own inside — the cards remain cards on the same board."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "inline": [
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "v": "Tags",
     "children": [
      {
       "t": "text",
       "v": "Tags"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "v": " cut across everything. A tag is not a location; the same card can carry several, and a tag's detail view gathers every board, group and card that carries it from anywhere in the workspace."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
